<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
	<!--
	  GENERATE_INFOPLIST_FILE merges the INFOPLIST_KEY_* build settings into
	  this file at build time, so simple keys belong there. This file is for
	  the nested structures that cannot be expressed as build settings.

	  CFBundleDocumentTypes is what replaces the share extension. Declaring the
	  types we accept puts Office Daze in the iOS share sheet's app row; iOS
	  copies the shared file into the app's inbox and launches us, and the app
	  handles it in onOpenURL. A share extension would have needed App Groups,
	  and App Groups needs a paid account.

	  NSLocation*UsageDescription are the strings iOS shows in the permission
	  prompts. When In Use is requested first and Always only once that is
	  granted — asking for Always cold gets denied.

	  UIBackgroundModes carries "location" because the handoff asks for it.
	  Strictly, region monitoring does not need it: iOS relaunches the app for
	  a region crossing regardless. It is here so the capability matches the
	  brief, not because the geofence would fail without it.
	-->
	<key>NSLocationWhenInUseUsageDescription</key>
	<string>Office Daze watches a 50m perimeter around your offices, so it can show you your desk number the moment you arrive.</string>
	<key>NSLocationAlwaysAndWhenInUseUsageDescription</key>
	<string>Always is what lets the arrival alert fire when Office Daze is closed — which is every time, since you will be walking in with the phone in your pocket. Your location is never sent anywhere; it never leaves the device.</string>
	<!--
	  Write-only, not full access. The booking screen adds an event and never
	  reads one, and iOS shows a lighter prompt for the smaller permission.
	-->
	<!--
	  The camera is the shortest path from a confirmation on a monitor to a
	  booking in the app: point, shoot, read. No photo-library key is needed
	  beside it — the picture is handed straight to the app and never saved.
	-->
	<key>NSCameraUsageDescription</key>
	<string>Photograph a desk booking on your screen and Office Daze reads the details off it. The picture is sent to Anthropic to be read by Claude, and is not saved to your photos.</string>

	<key>NSCalendarsWriteOnlyAccessUsageDescription</key>
	<string>Adding a desk booking to your calendar puts the office, the floor and the hours where the rest of your day already is. Office Daze only ever writes events; it cannot read your calendar.</string>

	<key>UIBackgroundModes</key>
	<array>
		<string>location</string>
	</array>

	<key>CFBundleDocumentTypes</key>
	<array>
		<dict>
			<key>CFBundleTypeName</key>
			<string>Booking Screenshot</string>
			<key>LSItemContentTypes</key>
			<array>
				<string>public.image</string>
			</array>
			<key>CFBundleTypeRole</key>
			<string>Viewer</string>
			<key>LSHandlerRank</key>
			<string>Alternate</string>
		</dict>
		<dict>
			<key>CFBundleTypeName</key>
			<string>Booking PDF</string>
			<key>LSItemContentTypes</key>
			<array>
				<string>com.adobe.pdf</string>
			</array>
			<key>CFBundleTypeRole</key>
			<string>Viewer</string>
			<key>LSHandlerRank</key>
			<string>Alternate</string>
		</dict>
	</array>
</dict>
</plist>
